WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
Most of Earth's carbon,
about 65,500 billion tonnes,

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.210
is stored in rocks.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.430
The oceans hold about 50 times
more carbon than the atmosphere.

4
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:18.450
Yet in 2024, the CO₂ in our air
reached 423.9 parts per million:

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.930
52 per cent above pre-industrial levels.

6
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.350
Power stations burn coal, oil and
gas: a little of that rock store.

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.930
Why does that matter so much?

8
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.810
Is it too small to count?

9
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.490
In this mission, you'll
map Earth's carbon stores,

10
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.730
and the flows that move
carbon between them.

11
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.530
Then you'll compare the fast
carbon cycle with the slow one.

12
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.150
Your mission: explain why burning a
little of Earth's rock store makes such a

13
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:45.950
difference.
